<h2>2026-08-14 — <code>/planning/daily</code>: Focus Queue populated + Start Day button works</h2>

<p><strong>Trigger:</strong> an Application Alert fired from <code>Planning.pm sub daily</code>:</p>
<pre>Priority ranking error: Can't locate object method "new" via package "Comserv::Util::TodoRanking"</pre>
<p>The Daily Priorities tab (🎯 Focus Queue) was rendering empty and the planning Projects query was failing — both silently swallowed by <code>eval</code>, so the page still returned HTTP 200.</p>

<h3>Root causes (3 independent bugs in <code>sub daily</code>)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Focus Queue ranking:</strong> <code>Comserv::Util::TodoRanking-&gt;new</code> — <code>TodoRanking</code> is a <em>procedural</em> module; scoring is the plain sub <code>Comserv::Util::TodoRanking::score_todo($h, $ctx)</code> (no constructor). The call also passed <code>($c, $t)</code> instead of a column hashref + ctx.</li>
    <li><strong>Focus Queue data:</strong> <code>$c-&gt;model('Todo')-&gt;get_all_todos_for_listing($c, $sitename)</code> — that method does not exist on <code>Comserv::Model::Todo</code> (only <code>get_top_todos</code>, <code>get_todos_for_date</code>, <code>get_all_todos_for_calendar</code>, <code>fetch_todo_record</code>). So <code>@all</code> was always empty.</li>
    <li><strong>Planning projects:</strong> <code>$c-&gt;model('Ency')-&gt;resultset('Project')</code> — <code>model('Ency')</code> is not a registered Catalyst model (returns <code>undef</code>), causing <em>"Can't call method resultset on an undefined value"</em>. Every other caller uses <code>model('DBEncy')</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixes</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> — <code>sub daily</code> Focus Queue block rewritten to fetch open (non-done) todos via <code>$schema-&gt;resultset('Todo')-&gt;search(...)</code> (site-filtered), build a <code>%row_by_id</code> column-hash map, score each with the procedural <code>Comserv::Util::TodoRanking::score_todo($h, { now_epoch =&gt; time() })</code>, sort by <code>ap_score</code>, and take the top 20 into <code>@active_priorities</code> (real row objects, as the template expects) with the rest into <code>@remaining_open_todos</code>. Both error paths keep their <code>log_with_details</code> calls (focus query vs focus rank/remaining) so failures still land in <code>application.log</code>.</li>
    <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> — planning-projects query changed from <code>model('Ency')</code> to <code>model('DBEncy')</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/js/planning/daily-plan-utils.js</code> — <code>dailyLogAction()</code> made null-safe: the rebuilt <code>DailyPlan.tt</code> index does not carry the old <code>dl-feedback</code> / <code>dl-start-btn</code> / <code>dl-end-btn</code> ids, so <code>feedback.textContent = …</code> threw <code>TypeError</code> before the <code>fetch</code> fired. Every <code>feedback</code>/<code>startBtn</code>/<code>endBtn</code> access is now guarded, so the Start Day / End Day POST always reaches <code>/planning/daily_log</code>.</li>
    <li><code>root/admin/planning/DailyPlan.tt</code> + <code>root/admin/planning/_today_work_tab.tt</code> — added the <code>&lt;span id="dl-feedback"&gt;</code> status node to both action cards so the user sees "Starting…" / success / error inline.</li>
    <li><code>root/static/css/planning/daily-plan.css</code> — added <code>.ActionBarFeedback</code> styling.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>perl -c lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code> → "syntax OK". No remaining calls to <code>TodoRanking-&gt;new</code>, <code>get_all_todos_for_listing</code>, or <code>model('Ency')</code> in the controller. Static JS/CSS and <code>.tt</code> recompile per request via <code>Module::Refresh</code> on the running <code>:3001</code> process (no restart performed, per ops rules).</p>

